---
The existing parser's AST rebuilt from the discovery stage's syntax trees: the
tree path's counterpart of `discovery_adapter.brp`, which rebuilds it from the
stage's tables. Declaration previews, whole assembled modules, expressions and
bodies each project to the parsed forms the existing typecheck consumes, so the
differential can compare the tree path with the existing parser span for span.

Nothing in the compiler imports this module: production reads the tables through
`discovery_adapter.brp`, so the tree parsers and this projection are not part of
`bin/blorp`. Only tests and the parity tools (`scripts/compiler-new-parity`) use
it. It joins the production adapter when the tree path becomes the stage's
default and the table path is deleted.

A tree that cannot be rebuilt is a `LegacyDeclarationPreviewError`, never a
default: no placeholder value flows into the rebuilt AST.
---
import:
	../compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/parse/tree_module_declaration_scan as TreeScan
	../compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/parse/tree_declaration_preview_parser as TreePreviews
	../compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/parse/tree_function_header_parser:
